 I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30164832376020423, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10612330822886319, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75787336, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3004170544075283, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11487700343932616, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73334384, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Authenticated node-replication handshake completes reliably between nodes.\\n\\n- Handshake succeeds under high-latency network conditions, not only nominal latency.\\n\\n- Blocking timeout issue is resolved before multi-site rollout can proceed.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-04**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because multi-site local deployments need distributed zero-trust node synchronization.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-22**: Diana - Handshake Timeout Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after validation showed handshake timeouts on high-latency networks; resolution depends on the encryption work bu