othing conclusive to report yet, I'll have the full inventory soon.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 39 slack thread licens audit channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 09 2026 08 09 11 13 diana start the third parti licens audit across the depend tree need a full inventori befor we sign off on anyth for releas 2026 08 09 12 37 alic watch close for gpl or agpl our client agreement rule out ship copyleft code in the core engin 2026 08 09 12 46 diana that s exact what i m scan for use licens checker against the depend manifest to flag anyth outsid mit apach bsd 2026 08 09 13 19 bob are you follow transit depend too a clean top level librari can still pull in someth restrict underneath 2026 08 09 13 24 diana yes do a recurs pas not just the direct depend 2026 08 09 13 51 evan want a hand with the docker base imag layer onc the app level scan is done 2026 08 09 14 07 diana that d help still work through the result noth conclus to report yet i ll have the full inventori soon\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e90df4e28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"id\": \"f45d87f25a79b4cd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2822770329027745, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10768188986110641, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6896657, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e90df4e28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1085, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:57\", \"token_count\": 310, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-36\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Path Handling\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:19] Evan**: Windows builds have been failing on path separators — the ingestion logic has backslash assumptions baked in that don't hold up on Windows.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:34] Bob**: Quick search-and-replace for the separator, or something more thorough?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:39] Evan**: More thorough — moving the path handling to be OS-aware instead of hardcoded, so this doesn't come back the next time we touch it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:41] Bob**: LGTM.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 12:46] Charlie**: What about the temp directory? I remember some older code assuming a Linux-style path there too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:00] Evan**: Already on it. Fixing that in the same pass so it respects the OS-level temp location instead of guessing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:01] Alice**: How's this looking for a first test build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:03] Evan**: Once the path fix holds up under test, I should be able to produce a build artifact from it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 36 slack thread window path handl channel releas date 2026 08 10 2026 08 1010 19 evan window build have been fail on path separ the ingest logic ha backslash assumpt bake in that don t hold up on window 2026 08 1010 34 bob quick search and replac for the separ or someth more thorough 2026 08 1010 39 evan more thorough move the path handl to be o awar instead of hardcod so this doesn t come back the next time we touch it 2026 08 1010 41 bob lgtm 2026 08 10 12 46 charli what about the temp directori i rememb some older code assum a linux style path there too 2026 08 10 13 00 evan alreadi on it fix that in the same pas so it respect the o level temp locat instead of guess 2026 08 10 13 01 alic how s this look for a first test build 2026 08 10 13 03 evan onc the path fix hold up under test i should be abl to produc a build artifact from it\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8fd13168a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"id\": \"861669a2b04e3fa7\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2800414629027745, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10768188986110641, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6822138, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8fd13168a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-10-windows-path-handling.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1051, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:11\", \"token_count\": 322, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Issue\\n\\nPath arguments containing backslashes (Windows-style, e.g. `C:\\\\docs\\\\input.pdf`) were mishandled by the CLI's path parser, which had only been exercised against forward-slash paths on Linux/macOS.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nPath arguments are now normalized to the platform-native separator before they reach the file-loading code, rather than assuming forward slashes everywhere.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers path-string handling only. It does not cover code signing or Windows Defender/SmartScreen behavior — those are separate, later concerns for CIPH-39 and are not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat issu path argument contain backslash window style e g c doc input pdf were mishandl by the cli s path parser which had onli been exercis against forward slash path on linux maco sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat fix path argument are now normal to the platform nativ separ befor they reach the file load code rather than assum forward slash everywher sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat scope this note cover path string handl onli it doe not cover code sign or window defend smartscreen behavior those are separ later concern for ciph 39 and are not address here